1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:08,628
This is BrewLab, an AI email support demo for a fictional coffee equipment store.

2
00:00:08,628 --> 00:00:15,037
This walkthrough uses real Gmail and Google Sheets screenshots from a completed test, with personal details redacted.

3
00:00:16,237 --> 00:00:19,363
One customer sent three emails within two minutes.

4
00:00:19,363 --> 00:00:23,662
The bot waited for the quiet period, then combined the questions.

5
00:00:23,662 --> 00:00:26,006
Only one conversation shows a draft.

6
00:00:26,006 --> 00:00:29,914
The number two is the conversation count, not two drafts.

7
00:00:31,237 --> 00:00:40,182
The single draft answers all three questions: seventy nine US dollars, Canadian shipping from twelve dollars, and delivery in five to nine business days.

8
00:00:40,182 --> 00:00:43,164
The reply stays in Gmail for human review.

9
00:00:45,237 --> 00:00:51,186
When the customer asks for a human agent, the bot applies the handoff and needs human labels.

10
00:00:51,186 --> 00:00:55,384
It prepares a short acknowledgment, while the original request is forwarded internally.

11
00:00:57,237 --> 00:01:01,575
The sent handoff message includes the original email as an attachment.

12
00:01:01,575 --> 00:01:04,336
The colleague can review the source request.

13
00:01:04,336 --> 00:01:08,674
This screen documents the sent message, not independent confirmation of receipt.

14
00:01:10,237 --> 00:01:12,874
Google Sheets records each processed incoming email.

15
00:01:12,874 --> 00:01:16,264
Three pricing rows belong to the single merged reply.

16
00:01:16,264 --> 00:01:18,901
The fourth row records the human handoff.

17
00:01:18,901 --> 00:01:23,044
All four used draft mode, and the error column is empty.

18
00:01:24,244 --> 00:01:28,826
The settings sheet controls the mode, schedule, tone, and escalation policy.

19
00:01:28,826 --> 00:01:30,909
The captured configuration is off.

20
00:01:30,909 --> 00:01:32,991
Earlier processing used draft mode.

21
00:01:32,991 --> 00:01:38,406
This is a configuration snapshot, not a live recording of a mode change.

22
00:01:39,606 --> 00:01:45,613
BrewLab combines message batching, knowledge based drafts, human escalation, and a spreadsheet audit trail.

23
00:01:45,613 --> 00:01:50,333
Explore the source code and setup guide in the public repository.
